{"surah": 109, "verses": [{"ayah": 1, "text": "قُلْ يَٰٓأَيُّهَا ٱلْكَٰفِرُونَ ", "translation": "Say, \"O disbelievers,", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "قُلْ", "translit": "ْlُq", "root": "قول"}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "يَٰٓأَيُّهَا", "translit": "āَhُّyَaʾَٰٓy", "root": "ايي"}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "ٱلْكَٰفِرُونَ", "translit": "َnwُrِfَٰkْlٱ", "root": "كفر"}], "hasIhya": true}, {"ayah": 2, "text": "لَآ أَعْبُدُ مَا تَعْبُدُونَ ", "translation": "I do not worship what you worship.", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "لَآ", "translit": "ٓāَl", "root": ""}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "أَعْبُدُ", "translit": "ُdُbْʿعَaʾ", "root": "عبد"}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "مَا", "translit": "āَm", "root": ""}, {"id": 4, "arabic": "تَعْبُدُونَ", "translit": "َnwُdُbْʿعَt", "root": "عبد"}], "hasIhya": false}, {"ayah": 3, "text": "وَلَآ أَنتُمْ عَٰبِدُونَ مَآ أَعْبُدُ ", "translation": "Nor are you worshippers of what I worship.", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "وَلَآ", "translit": "ٓāَlَw", "root": ""}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "أَنتُمْ", "translit": "ْmُtnَaʾ", "root": ""}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "عَٰبِدُونَ", "translit": "َnwُdِbَٰʿع", "root": "عبد"}, {"id": 4, "arabic": "مَآ", "translit": "ٓāَm", "root": ""}, {"id": 5, "arabic": "أَعْبُدُ", "translit": "ُdُbْʿعَaʾ", "root": "عبد"}], "hasIhya": false}, {"ayah": 4, "text": "وَلَآ أَنَا۠ عَابِدٌ مَّا عَبَدتُّمْ ", "translation": "Nor will I be a worshipper of what you worship.", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "وَلَآ", "translit": "ٓāَlَw", "root": ""}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "أَنَا۠", "translit": "۠āَnَaʾ", "root": ""}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "عَابِدٌ", "translit": "ٌdِbāَʿع", "root": "عبد"}, {"id": 4, "arabic": "مَّا", "translit": "āَّm", "root": ""}, {"id": 5, "arabic": "عَبَدتُّمْ", "translit": "ْmُّtdَbَʿع", "root": "عبد"}], "hasIhya": false}, {"ayah": 5, "text": "وَلَآ أَنتُمْ عَٰبِدُونَ مَآ أَعْبُدُ ", "translation": "Nor will you be worshippers of what I worship.", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "وَلَآ", "translit": "ٓāَlَw", "root": ""}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "أَنتُمْ", "translit": "ْmُtnَaʾ", "root": ""}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "عَٰبِدُونَ", "translit": "َnwُdِbَٰʿع", "root": "عبد"}, {"id": 4, "arabic": "مَآ", "translit": "ٓāَm", "root": ""}, {"id": 5, "arabic": "أَعْبُدُ", "translit": "ُdُbْʿعَaʾ", "root": "عبد"}], "hasIhya": false}, {"ayah": 6, "text": "لَكُمْ دِينُكُمْ وَلِىَ دِينِ ", "translation": "For you is your religion, and for me is my religion.\"", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "لَكُمْ", "translit": "ْmُkَl", "root": ""}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "دِينُكُمْ", "translit": "ْmُkُnyِd", "root": "دين"}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "وَلِىَ", "translit": "َàِlَw", "root": ""}, {"id": 4, "arabic": "دِينِ", "translit": "ِnyِd", "root": "دين"}], "hasIhya": false}], "tafsir": {"1": [{"arabic": "بأن يصلي ركعتين يقرأ في الأولى فاتحة الكتاب وقل يا أيها الكافرون وفي الثانية الفاتحة وقل هو الله أحد فإذا فرغ دعا وقال اللهم إني أستخيرك بعلمك وأستقدرك بقدرتك وأسألك من فضلك العظيم فإنك تقدر ولا أقدر وتعلم ولا أعلم وأنت علام الغيوب اللهم إن كنت تعلم أن هذا الأمر خير لي في ديني ودنياي وعاقبة أمري وعاجله وآجله فاقدره لي وبارك لي فيه ثم يسره لي وإن كنت تعلم أن هذا الأمر شر لي في ديني ودنياي وعاقبة أمري وعاجله وآجله فاصرفني عنه واصرفه عني واقدر لي الخير أينما كان إنك على كل شيء قدير (6) رواه جابر بن عبد الله قال ك", "english": "**QUAD_ANCHORS:**\n- Root: خسف (kha-sa-fa)\n  * Lisan / Ayn: [Core linguistic root meaning] To swallow up, to cause to sink into the earth; the darkening of the sun or moon (khusūf for the moon, kusūf for the sun, though both are used interchangeably)\n  * Al-Raghib (Mufradat): [Theological/Kalam semantic nuance] The eclipse as a divine sign (āyah) — not a natural phenomenon merely, but a portent summoning the servant to remembrance of God\n  * Al-Zamakhshari (Asas): [Literal vs Metaphorical distinction] Literal: the celestial bodies being veiled/obscured; Metaphorical: the veiling of hearts from divine remembrance\n- Root: سقى (sa-qa)\n  * Lisan / Ayn: [Core linguistic root meaning] To give to drink, to water; istisqā' — the act of seeking rain/water from God\n  * Al-Raghib (Mufradat): [Theological/Kalam semantic nuance] The prayer for rain as a communal acknowledgment of absolute dependence upon divine providence\n  * Al-Zamakhshari (Asas): [Literal vs Metaphorical distinction] Literal: requesting water; Metaphorical: seeking divine mercy and abundance\n- Root: جنز (ja-na-za)\n  * Lisan / Ayn: [Core linguistic root meaning] The bier/corpse; janāzah — the funeral\n  * Al-Raghib (Mufradat): [Theological/Kalam semantic nuance] The funeral prayer as a collective obligation (farḍ kifāyah) — the living standing as intercessors for the dead\n  * Al-Zamakhshari (Asas): [Literal vs Metaphorical distinction] Literal: the bier upon which the dead is carried; Metaphorical: the entire funeral rite as a reminder of one's own mortality\n- Root: حيي (ḥa-ya)\n  * Lisan / Ayn: [Core linguistic root meaning] To live; taḥiyyah — greeting, salutation; the \"greeting of the mosque\" (taḥiyyat al-masjid)\n  * Al-Raghib (Mufradat): [Theological/Kalam semantic nuance] The greeting of the mosque as an act of reverence for the sacred space — a spiritual courtesy toward the house of God\n  * Al-Zamakhshari (Asas): [Literal vs Metaphorical distinction] Literal: greeting a person; Metaphorical: greeting the mosque through prayer as one greets a host upon entering his abode\n- Root: خير (kha-ya-ra)\n  * Lisan / Ayn: [Core linguistic root meaning] To choose; istikhārah — seeking divine choice/guidance\n  * Al-Raghib (Mufradat): [Theological/Kalam semantic nuance] The prayer of seeking guidance as the servant's acknowledgment that only God knows the unseen consequences of affairs\n  * Al-Zamakhshari (Asas): [Literal vs Metaphorical distinction] Literal: asking someone to choose for you; Metaphorical: delegating one's affairs to divine providence while abandoning personal preference\n- Root: ركع (ra-ka-ʿa)\n  * Lisan / Ayn: [Core linguistic root meaning] To bow; rukūʿ — the bowing posture in prayer\n  * Al-Raghib (Mufradat): [Theological/Kalam semantic nuance] Bowing as physical expression of humility and submission before divine majesty\n  * Al-Zamakhshari (Asas): [Literal vs Metaphorical distinction] Literal: the bodily posture of inclination; Metaphorical: the spiritual posture of humble submission — \"Sheikhs bowing with age\" and \"camels bowing with exhaustion\"\n- Sibawayh Rule: باب الحصر والتقييد (Restriction & Focused Predication) — The conditional constructions (idhā... fa...) governing the temporal and circumstantial clauses for when these prayers become incumbent or recommended", "book_title": "Arrangement of Litanies", "section_title_ar": "Section 164", "section_title_en": "Section 164", "section_index": 164, "anchors": "*(Anchors established)*", "content_type": "dua", "topic": "Al-Ghazali on supplications, prayers, and their spiritual power, from 'Arrangement of Litanies'", "badge": "Du'a"}, {"arabic": "وفي الصبح في السفر قل يا أيها الكافرون وقل هو الله أحد وكذلك في ركعتي الفجر والطواف والتحية وهو في جميع ذلك مستديم للقيام ووضع اليدين كما وصفنا في أول الصلاة الركوع ولواحقه ثم يركع ويراعي فيه أمورا وهو أن يكبر للركوع وأن يرفع يديه مع تكبيرة الركوع وأن يمد التكبير مدا إلى الانتهاء إلى الركوع وأن يضع راحتيه على ركبتيه في الركوع وأصابعه منشورة موجهة نحو القبلة على طول الساق وأن ينصب ركبتيه ولا يثنيهما وأن يمد ظهره مستويا وأن يكون عنقه ورأسه مستويين مع ظهره كالصفيحة الواحدة ل", "english": "I say: Then the worshipper begins with the opening supplication (duʿāʾ al-istiftāḥ). It is excellent that he say, following his utterance of \"Allāhu akbar, Allāhu akbar\": \"Kabīran wa-l-ḥamdu lillāhi kathīran wa-subḥāna Allāhi bukratan wa-aṣīlā\" (Great indeed is Allah, and abundant praise be to Allah, and glory be to Allah morning and evening) {«الله أكبر كبيرا والحمد لله كثيرا وسبحان الله بكرة وأصيلا»} — then: \"Wajjahtu wajhiya...\" (I have turned my face...) up to his saying \"...wa-anā min al-muslimīn\" (and I am among those who submit) {«وجهت وجهي إلى قوله وأنا من المسلمين»}. Then he says: \"Subḥānaka Allāhumma wa-bi-ḥamdika wa-tabāraka-smuka wa-taʿālā jadduka wa-jalla thanāʾuka wa-lā ilāha ghayruk\" (Glory be to You, O Allah, and with Your praise; blessed is Your Name and exalted is Your majesty; glorious is Your praise and there is no god but You) {«سبحانك اللهم وبحمدك وتبارك اسمك وتعالى جدك وجل ثناؤك ولا إله غيرك»} — so that he may combine within himself the various dispersed reports transmitted in the traditions.", "book_title": "Mysteries of Hajj", "section_title_ar": "Section 127", "section_title_en": "Section 127 — On the Recitation (Qirāʾah) and the Bowing (Rukūʿ) with Its Attendant Matters", "section_index": 127, "anchors": "- Root: قرأ (Qaraʾa)\n  * Lisan / Ayn: Core meaning of gathering and assembling letters into articulated speech; recitation as the oral articulation of written or memorized text.\n  * Al-Raghib (Mufradat): In the Quranic and liturgical context, qirāʾah is the deliberate, worshipful utterance of the divine word, distinct from mere reading; it is an act of devotion requiring presence of heart.\n  * Al-Zamakhshari (Asas): Literal (ḥaqīqah) usage denotes the physical articulation of sounds; metaphorical (majāz) usage extends to the inward recitation of the heart in contemplation.\n- Root: ركع (Rakaʿa)\n  * Lisan / Ayn: The physical act of bowing; the bending of the back in humility.\n  * Al-Raghib (Mufradat): \"الركوع: الانحناء، فتارة يستعمل في الهيئة المخصوصة في الصلاة كما هي، وتارة في التواضع والتذلل\" — The bowing is an inclination, used sometimes for the specific posture in prayer, and sometimes for humility and self-abasement.\n  * Al-Zamakhshari (Asas): Literal (ḥaqīqah): \"شيخ راكع: منحن من الكبر\" — an old man bowed with age. Metaphorical (majāz): \"لغبت الإبل حتى ركعت\" — camels fatigued until they lowered their heads, indicating the physical posture as the outward sign of inward submission.\n- Root: صبح (Ṣabaḥa)\n  * Al-Raghib (Al-Mufradat): \"الصبح والصباح، أول النهار\" — the dawn is the beginning of the day, the time when the horizon reddens.\n  * Al-Zamakhshari (Asas - Majaz/Metaphorical): \"أصبح يا رجل: انتبه من غفلتك\" — \"become awake, O man: awaken from your heedlessness,\" showing the dawn prayer as the time of spiritual awakening.\n- Sibawayh Rule: Rule of Prepositional Interposition (باب الفصل بين الجار والمجرور) — governing the permissible separation between governing and governed elements, applied here to the proper pausing (waqf) and connecting (waṣl) of Quranic phrases to preserve meaning.", "content_type": "dhikr", "topic": "Al-Ghazali on constant remembrance of God and contemplative invocations, from 'Mysteries of Hajj'", "badge": "Dhikr"}]}, "wordTiming": {"minshawi": {"1": [[1, 500, 946], [2, 946, 4228], [3, 4228, 5960]], "109:1": [[1, 500, 946], [2, 946, 4228], [3, 4228, 5960]], "2": [[1, 280, 2122], [2, 2122, 3023], [3, 3023, 3772], [4, 3772, 5320]], "109:2": [[1, 280, 2122], [2, 2122, 3023], [3, 3023, 3772], [4, 3772, 5320]], "3": [[1, 370, 2851], [2, 2851, 3757], [3, 3757, 5407], [4, 5407, 7370], [5, 7370, 8330]], "109:3": [[1, 370, 2851], [2, 2851, 3757], [3, 3757, 5407], [4, 5407, 7370], [5, 7370, 8330]], "4": [[1, 470, 2569], [2, 2569, 3464], [3, 3464, 4550], [4, 4550, 5445], [5, 5445, 6540]], "109:4": [[1, 470, 2569], [2, 2569, 3464], [3, 3464, 4550], [4, 4550, 5445], [5, 5445, 6540]], "5": [[1, 180, 2592], [2, 2592, 3473], [3, 3473, 5078], [4, 5078, 6987], [5, 6987, 7920]], "109:5": [[1, 180, 2592], [2, 2592, 3473], [3, 3473, 5078], [4, 5078, 6987], [5, 6987, 7920]], "6": [[1, 200, 865], [2, 865, 2285], [3, 2285, 3394], [4, 3394, 4370]], "109:6": [[1, 200, 865], [2, 865, 2285], [3, 2285, 3394], [4, 3394, 4370]]}, "abdulbasit": {"1": [[1, 950, 1150], [2, 1160, 3610], [3, 3620, 5220]], "109:1": [[1, 950, 1150], [2, 1160, 3610], [3, 3620, 5220]], "2": [[1, 500, 1630], [2, 1640, 2510], [3, 2520, 2850], [4, 2860, 4220]], "109:2": [[1, 500, 1630], [2, 1640, 2510], [3, 2520, 2850], [4, 2860, 4220]], "3": [[1, 600, 2530], [2, 2540, 3920], [3, 3930, 5290], [4, 5300, 5400], [5, 5410, 7450]], "109:3": [[1, 600, 2530], [2, 2540, 3920], [3, 3930, 5290], [4, 5300, 5400], [5, 5410, 7450]], "4": [[1, 550, 2230], [2, 2240, 2580], [3, 2590, 4480], [4, 4490, 4710], [5, 4720, 5990]], "109:4": [[1, 550, 2230], [2, 2240, 2580], [3, 2590, 4480], [4, 4490, 4710], [5, 4720, 5990]], "5": [[1, 700, 2430], [2, 2440, 3920], [3, 3930, 5320], [4, 5330, 5430], [5, 5440, 7370]], "109:5": [[1, 700, 2430], [2, 2440, 3920], [3, 3930, 5320], [4, 5330, 5430], [5, 5440, 7370]], "6": [[1, 650, 1180], [2, 1190, 2110], [3, 2120, 2830], [4, 2840, 3470]], "109:6": [[1, 650, 1180], [2, 1190, 2110], [3, 2120, 2830], [4, 2840, 3470]]}, "abdulbasit_mujawwad": {"1": [[1, 3100, 3440], [2, 3450, 7920], [3, 7930, 13170]], "109:1": [[1, 3100, 3440], [2, 3450, 7920], [3, 7930, 13170]], "2": [[1, 3270, 6000], [2, 6010, 7600], [3, 7610, 8500], [4, 8510, 14660]], "109:2": [[1, 3270, 6000], [2, 6010, 7600], [3, 7610, 8500], [4, 8510, 14660]], "3": [[1, 2850, 5830], [2, 5840, 6800], [3, 6810, 9520], [4, 9530, 10980], [5, 10990, 12140]], "109:3": [[1, 2850, 5830], [2, 5840, 6800], [3, 6810, 9520], [4, 9530, 10980], [5, 10990, 12140]], "4": [[1, 2890, 5080], [2, 5090, 5620], [3, 5630, 8370], [4, 8380, 9110], [5, 9120, 12510]], "109:4": [[1, 2890, 5080], [2, 5090, 5620], [3, 5630, 8370], [4, 8380, 9110], [5, 9120, 12510]], "5": [[1, 2240, 4520], [2, 4530, 6540], [3, 6550, 9260], [4, 9270, 10990], [5, 11000, 13390]], "109:5": [[1, 2240, 4520], [2, 4530, 6540], [3, 6550, 9260], [4, 9270, 10990], [5, 11000, 13390]], "6": [[1, 3050, 3790], [2, 3800, 6370], [3, 6380, 10090], [4, 10100, 11650]], "109:6": [[1, 3050, 3790], [2, 3800, 6370], [3, 6380, 10090], [4, 10100, 11650]]}, "abdulbasit_warsh": {"1": [[1, 450, 1185], [2, 1185, 4428], [3, 4428, 7270]], "109:1": [[1, 450, 1185], [2, 1185, 4428], [3, 4428, 7270]], "2": [[1, 450, 1677], [2, 1677, 3615], [3, 3615, 4519], [4, 4519, 6748]], "109:2": [[1, 450, 1677], [2, 1677, 3615], [3, 3615, 4519], [4, 45